            <ArticleTitle>Metastatic compression fractures--vertebroplasty for pain control.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Quality of life issues remain at the forefront for individuals with life-threatening disease, such as metastatic cancer. The pain of metastatic bone cancer can severely hamper an individual's quality of life. Percutaneous vertebroplasty offers a minimally invasive way to reinforce bony elements, provide substantial improvement in pain control, allow for mobilization, and overall improve quality of life in these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
